    "content": "# P2.6 \u2014 Audio device & I/O settings\n\n## Context (read this before touching anything)\n\nThis lands after P2.5 (Transport now runs sample-accurate off the real audio\ncallback \u2014 see `docs/plans/audio/README.md` and\n`docs/plans/audio/P2.5-transport-prompt.md`) and before P3 (Notes/Synths/\nEffects). It is new scope, not in `docs/plans/audio/README.md`'s original\nphase list \u2014 the user asked for it directly because right now there is no\nway to pick an audio device, sample rate, or buffer size at all, which\nmatters before P3's synths need to be heard through real hardware.\n\n**Confirmed, current state (verified against the live code this session):**\n\n- `AudioEngine::Start()` (`src/audio/AudioEngine.cpp:35-42`) calls\n  `Platform::AudioDeviceOpen(...)` and takes whatever sample rate comes\n  back. No device is chosen.\n- `Platform::AudioDeviceOpen` (`src/platform/Platform.mm:1848-1900`)\n  constructs a fresh `AVAudioEngine`, reads `[mixer outputFormatForBus:0]`\n  (i.e. whatever the *system's current default output device* reports), and\n  starts it. There is no device enumeration, no `AudioDeviceID` selection,\n  no requested sample rate, no requested buffer size, anywhere in this path.\n- **A second, unrelated `AVAudioEngine` instance already exists** at\n  `Platform.mm:1595-1657` (`AudioStart`/`AudioStop`/`AudioIsRunning`/\n  `AudioDeviceName`, using file-local `gEngine`/`gRunning`/`gDeviceName`/\n  `gLiveAnalyser`). This is a pre-existing, older feature \u2014 a live\n  microphone level/FFT analyser, unrelated to the new synth engine \u2014 that\n  taps `[gEngine inputNode]` for its *own* separate mic capture. It has\n  nothing to do with `AudioEngine`/`AudioNode`/P0-P2.5's work. **Decide\n  explicitly (see Open decisions below) whether this phase's new \"audio\n  input device\" setting governs this pre-existing capture path too, or is\n  scoped only to the new synth engine's future audio-input nodes** \u2014 do not\n  silently assume one or the other.\n- There is no settings/preferences persistence mechanism anywhere in this\n  codebase. Global UI toggles like `gSnapToGrid`/`gGridSnap`\n  (`src/main.cpp:261-262`) are plain in-memory globals that reset to their\n  compiled-in defaults every launch \u2014 they are never written to or read\n  from disk, not even inside the patch file. The existing \"Menu\" top-level\n  ImGui menu (`src/main.cpp:8672-8700`, inside the `BeginMenuBar()` block\n  starting `:8605`) is the precedent for how app-level (not per-patch)\n  settings are exposed: a `BeginMenu(\"Menu\")`/`SeparatorText(...)` section\n  with widgets bound directly to global variables, no separate window.\n\n## What this phase adds\n\n1. **CoreAudio HAL device enumeration.** `AVAudioEngine` alone cannot select\n   a non-default output device on macOS \u2014 you have to reach through to the\n   underlying `AudioUnit` (`[engine outputNode].AUAudioUnit` /\n   `kAudioOutputUnitProperty_CurrentDevice` via `AudioUnitSetProperty`) or\n   use `AudioObjectGetPropertyData` with `kAudioHardwarePropertyDevices` /\n   `kAudioObjectPropertyScopeGlobal` directly against `AudioObjectID`s. Add\n   this enumeration (device name + `AudioDeviceID` + is-input/is-output,\n   via `kAudioDevicePropertyStreamConfiguration`) as new `Platform`\n   functions:\n   ```cpp\n   struct AudioDeviceInfo { std::string name; uint32_t deviceId; bool isInput; bool isOutput; };\n   std::vector<AudioDeviceInfo> AudioListDevices();\n   ```\n   Add this to the `Platform` namespace declared in `src/platform/Platform.h`\n   (near the existing `AudioDeviceOpen`/`AudioDeviceClose` declarations at\n   `:190-191`) with the implementation in `Platform.mm`.\n\n2. **Device/sample-rate/buffer-size selection on the new synth engine.**\n   Extend `Platform::AudioDeviceOpen`'s signature to accept an optional\n   requested output `AudioDeviceID` (0 = system default, preserving current\n   behavior), requested sample rate, and requested buffer (frame) size:\n   ```cpp\n   bool AudioDeviceOpen(AudioRenderCallback callback, void* userData,\n                        double& outSampleRate, std::string& outError,\n                        uint32_t requestedDeviceId = 0,\n                        double requestedSampleRate = 0.0,\n                        int requestedBufferFrames = 0);\n   ```\n   Setting a non-default device requires calling\n   `AudioUnitSetProperty(... kAudioOutputUnitProperty_CurrentDevice ...)` on\n   `h->engine.outputNode.audioUnit` **before** `[h->engine startAndReturnError:]`.\n   Setting sample rate / buffer size on macOS is a **device-wide, not\n   app-scoped** property \u2014 you set `kAudioDevicePropertyNominalSampleRate`\n   and `kAudioDevicePropertyBufferFrameSize` on the `AudioDeviceID` itself\n   via `AudioObjectSetPropertyData`, which affects every app using that\n   device system-wide until changed again. **State this tradeoff plainly in\n   the UI** (e.g. a one-line note near the buffer-size control) rather than\n   changing it silently \u2014 this is a real, surprising-if-undocumented macOS\n   quirk, not a bug to hide.\n   Requested values that the device rejects (unsupported sample rate,\n   clamped buffer size) should fall back to whatever the device actually\n   reports after the request, the same way the current code already reads\n   back `format.sampleRate` post-open rather than assuming the request\n   succeeded verbatim.\n\n3. **Oversampling: scope this narrowly.** There is no existing global\n   oversampling mechanism, and the plan's own \u00a73 Effects table already\n   scopes 4\u00d7 oversampling as a **per-effect** concern (Drive: \"4\u00d7 oversampled\",\n   `README.md:159`), not a device-level setting \u2014 a global oversampling\n   toggle doesn't have a clear target yet since no DSP nodes exist to\n   consume it (P3 hasn't landed). Add a single global `float gAudioOversample`\n   default `1.0f` (values `1`/`2`/`4`) stored the same way as the other new\n   settings in this phase (see item 5), wired nowhere yet \u2014 this phase's job\n   is to make the *setting* exist and be visible, not to make anything act\n   on it. Say explicitly in your summary that no node reads this yet \u2014 it's\n   a placeholder P3c's Drive/AudioFilter kernels will read once they exist,\n   not a claim that oversampling is implemented.\n\n4. **Wire it into `AudioEngine::Start()`.** `AudioEngine::Start()`\n   (`AudioEngine.cpp:35`) needs the three new settings values to pass\n   through to `Platform::AudioDeviceOpen`. Add matching fields/setters to\n   `AudioEngine` (mirroring how `mSampleRate` already exists at\n   `AudioEngine.h`) so the UI layer in `main.cpp` can set the selection\n   before calling `Start()`, without `main.cpp` reaching into `Platform`\n   directly (keep the existing layering \u2014 `main.cpp` talks to `AudioEngine`,\n   `AudioEngine` talks to `Platform`).\n\n5. **UI: an \"Audio\" section in the existing \"Menu\" menu.** Follow the exact\n   precedent at `main.cpp:8672-8700` \u2014 no new window, no new persistence\n   format (none exists in this codebase yet; introducing one is out of\n   scope for this phase, see Open decisions). Add a `SeparatorText(\"Audio\")`\n   block with:\n   - A combo box listing `Platform::AudioListDevices()`'s output devices\n     (default = whatever's currently active).\n   - A combo box listing `Platform::AudioListDevices()`'s input devices\n     (wire it through even though nothing yet consumes an input device on\n     the new engine \u2014 same \"setting exists before the thing that reads it\"\n     pattern as item 3).\n   - Sample rate as a combo of the standard set (44100/48000/88200/96000)\n     rather than free text \u2014 matches how `AVAudioFormat`/CoreAudio actually\n     negotiate rates, and avoids a text field that can hold nonsense.\n   - Buffer size similarly as a combo (64/128/256/512/1024/2048), with the\n     device-wide caveat from item 2 shown as `ImGui::TextDisabled` under it.\n   - The oversampling placeholder from item 3, as a combo (1\u00d7/2\u00d7/4\u00d7), with\n     a `TextDisabled` note that no node uses it yet.\n   - Changing device/sample-rate/buffer-size while the engine is already\n     running (`AudioEngine::Instance().Start()` already called \u2014 check via\n     the existing `SampleRate() > 0.0` pattern used elsewhere) must\n     `Stop()` then `Start()` again with the new settings rather than trying\n     to hot-swap a live `AVAudioEngine`. Show the actual post-open sample\n     rate/buffer size Platform reports back (not just the requested one) so\n     a rejected request is visible instead of silently wrong.\n\n## Open decisions \u2014 you decide, state your reasoning, don't silently pick\n\n- **Does the new \"input device\" selector also govern the pre-existing mic\n  analyser at `Platform.mm:1595-1657`?** Two reasonable answers: (a) yes,\n  thread the selected `AudioDeviceID` into `AudioStart()` too, unifying\n  device selection across both engines; (b) no, leave that path on system\n  default for now and scope this phase's input-device setting purely to\n  the new synth engine (which has no audio-input nodes yet anyway \u2014 P3\n  territory). Recommendation: **(b)**, it's less code and doesn't risk\n  regressing a working, unrelated feature for a setting nothing currently\n  consumes \u2014 but say explicitly which you picked and why in your summary.\n- **Should these settings persist across launches?** Recommendation: **no,\n  not this phase** \u2014 there is zero precedent for settings persistence\n  anywhere in this codebase (confirmed: `gSnapToGrid` et al. are\n  session-only), and inventing the first-ever preferences file format\n  should be its own deliberate decision, not a side effect of this phase.\n  Default to system default device / device-native sample rate / 512-frame\n  buffer / 1\u00d7 oversampling every launch, same as today's implicit behavior.\n\n## Explicitly out of scope\n\n- Anything about `OutputNode`/recording/export (that's the next phase,\n  P2.7 \u2014 wiring the live synthesized audio graph into\n  `src/nodes/OutputNode.cpp`'s recorder, which currently only reads\n  `AudioFileNode`-backed files off disk, not a live render).\n- The audio-analyse-as-modulator node \u2014 this already has a direct precedent\n  (`ImageAnalyzeNode`, `src/nodes/AnalyzeNodes.h:18-80`, `IModulator`\n  `Tap`/`ModulatorOutput()` pattern) and belongs in P3d per\n  `README.md:344-346` (\"Envelope Follower \u2192 modulator\"), not here.\n- Any node/DSP consuming the oversampling setting \u2014 see item 3.\n- Settings persistence \u2014 see Open decisions.\n\n## Build & verify\n\n```bash\ncmake --build build -j\"$(sysctl -n hw.ncpu)\"\n```\nConfirm clean build. Then run the full hygiene suite (this phase touches\n`main.cpp` and `Platform.mm` but no node-graph/cable code, so no new\n`INFINITE_*TEST` fixture is required \u2014 but a regression in unrelated areas\nwould still show up here):\n```bash\n.claude/skills/run-infinite-hygiene/driver.sh\n```\nExpect the same baseline as every prior phase: all checks pass except\n`PHASEATEST` (pre-existing, unrelated `\"Smooth\"` node-name collision \u2014\nalready known, do not attempt to fix it). Also re-run:\n```bash\nINFINITE_DSPTEST=1 ./build/Infinite.app/Contents/MacOS/Infinite\n```\nand confirm it still ends `DSPTEST OK` \u2014 this phase changes\n`Platform::AudioDeviceOpen`'s signature, which `AudioEngine::Start()` calls,\nso a broken default-path fallback would likely show up here first even\nthough DSPTEST itself uses `ProcessOffline`, not the live device.\n\nFinally, manually launch the app, open the \"Menu\" menu, confirm the new\n\"Audio\" section lists real device names for this machine, and confirm\nswitching output device/sample rate/buffer size doesn't crash or silently\nfail \u2014 check the post-open readback values actually reflect the change."
