    "deleted_in_commit": "72b371b7e37368b53ce00c425997b3504d24db06",
    "commit_info": "n1m21n|Sun Aug 16 18:42:24 2026 +0530|Remove experimental web-hand-synth test app",
    "content": "# P2.7 \u2014 Audio node UI system + reference Oscillator\n\n## Why this phase exists\n\nThis is new scope, inserted between P2.5 and P3 at the user's request. It is\n**not** in `docs/plans/audio/README.md`'s original phase list.\n\nThe trigger: P2 shipped three minimal proof nodes (Oscillator/Gain/Audio Out)\nto prove the cable plumbing. Rendered in the editor they look nothing like a\nprofessional DAW/modular instrument \u2014 and inspecting *why* turned up four\nstructural problems that would each be multiplied by ~30 if P3 started now.\nThis phase fixes the system, then proves it by building one genuinely complex\nnode (the real Oscillator) on top of it.\n\nThis is the same argument the plan already makes for \"P2 before P3\"\n(`README.md` \u00a75): it is the phase that *reduces* future cost. Building 30\naudio nodes on the current node-body layout produces 30 sparse nodes and 30\nhand-written param functions.\n\n## Confirmed current state \u2014 verified against live code, do not re-derive\n\n**Node body layout is an image-compositor layout.** Every node that isn't\nspecially cased draws a square image preview then a vertical stack of\nfull-width sliders:\n- `DrawPreview(INode*)` \u2014 `src/main.cpp:4889`. Draws a checkerboard backdrop\n  at `kPreviewSize` (190.0f, `main.cpp:104`), blits `GetOutputTexture()`, and\n  falls back to a literal `\"no input\"` string (`main.cpp:4919`) when the\n  texture is 0.\n- It is reached from the final `else` of the node-body dispatch at\n  `main.cpp:13556-13557`. **Audio nodes hit that `else`**, which is why an\n  Oscillator currently renders a 190px empty checkerboard reading \"no input\"\n  \u2014 it has no texture and never will.\n- The precedent for opting out is `GeometryNode`'s branch immediately above\n  (`main.cpp:13531-13549`): geometry emits a mesh, not a picture, so it draws\n  a compact info box instead. **Audio nodes need the equivalent, but richer.**\n\n**Only one param widget shape exists.** `ModSlider` (`main.cpp:563`) is\nfull-width (`kParamWidth` = 168.0f, `main.cpp:121`) and draws its own\nmodulator input pin. `DropdownButton` (`main.cpp:420`) is likewise\nfull-width. There is no compact, grid, or multi-column variant anywhere.\n\n**Params are one long `dynamic_cast` else-if chain** at\n`main.cpp:~13640-13760`, one branch per node type, each calling a hand-written\n`DrawXxxParams` function. There are already ~60 branches. Thirty audio nodes\nnaively added means thirty more.\n\n**`CanShowInViewportPanel` (`main.cpp:5093`) is a blocklist defaulting to\n`true`.** Every new node type must remember to opt out or it silently gets\n\"Open in viewport panel\" / \"Open in new window\" menu items that show a blank\nbox. Audio nodes were already excluded generically in a small fix immediately\npreceding this phase (`main.cpp:5106-5112`, gated on\n`dynamic_cast<IAudioSource*>` or `AudioInputSlot(0) != nullptr`) \u2014 **that fix\nis already in the tree; do not redo it.** Note its comment: P3d's Scope node\nis the deliberate future exception, since its spectrum mode does emit a real\nimage texture.\n\n**The right-click menu is shared with inline type gates.** `main.cpp:14654-14711`:\nHide/Show params, a Show/Hide viewport toggle gated on\n`dynamic_cast<IGeometrySource*>` (`:14664`), Open in viewport panel, Open in\nnew window, Help. There is no per-node-family policy concept.\n\n**Per-node UI flags already persist.** `GraphNode` (`src/core/GraphNode.h:36,42`)\ncarries `showParams` (defaults false) and `showMiniViewport`. They round-trip\nthrough the patch file's `flags` line \u2014 written at `src/core/Patch.cpp:197-198`,\nread at `:294-301` as exactly three whitespace-delimited ints.\n\n## Design decisions \u2014 already made by the user, implement these, do not re-litigate\n\n1. **Compact grid + expandable.** An audio node shows a small set of the most\n   important params in a **multi-column compact grid**, plus one visualizer.\n   An expand affordance reveals the full param set. Collapsed state keeps\n   large patches readable; expanded state is where the user actually dials in\n   a sound.\n2. **Exactly one inline visualizer per node, relevant to that node.** Not a\n   generic image preview. Oscillator \u2192 waveform trace. A filter \u2192 frequency\n   response curve. An envelope \u2192 its ADSR shape. A meter/scope \u2192 its level or\n   spectrum. Pick one per node type; do not stack three.\n3. **No image viewport for audio nodes. No \"Open in new window\". No \"Open in\n   viewport panel\".** Already enforced by the `CanShowInViewportPanel` gate\n   described above. Do not add an audio-node projector-window path.\n4. **Musically dense.** Every param a serious user would expect should exist\n   on the node, reachable via expansion. Sparse is the failure mode being\n   corrected here. See the researched inventory below.\n\n## Researched param inventory for the reference Oscillator\n\nCompiled from current commercial/open synth references (Bitwig Polymer,\nKilohearts Phase Plant, Ableton, Omnisphere, HALion FM, SynthEdit HD\nOscillator) \u2014 see Sources at the bottom. This is the target for \"musically\ndense\"; it is a *menu to choose from with justification*, not a mandate to\nship all 20 controls.\n\n**Tier 1 \u2014 collapsed view (the compact grid, ~4-6 controls):**\n- `waveform` \u2014 sine / triangle / saw / square / pulse / white / pink / brown\n  (the plan's \u00a73 Oscillator already specifies noise types live here, not in a\n  separate Noise node)\n- `frequency` (Hz) or pitch, depending on whether a note cable is connected\n- `volume` / level\n- `pulseWidth` (meaningful only for pulse/square \u2014 grey it out otherwise)\n- `unison` voice count\n- `detune` (cents)\n\n**Tier 2 \u2014 revealed on expand:**\n- `octave`, `semi`, `fine` \u2014 coarse/fine tuning, standard on every synth\n- `phase` \u2014 initial phase, and `phaseRandomize` / spread across unison voices\n- `stereoWidth` \u2014 unison voice stereo spread\n- `sync` \u2014 hard sync (off / internal ratio); pairs naturally with pulse waves\n- **2-op FM section**: `fmRatio` + `fmIndex`. The plan's \u00a73 explicitly scopes\n  Oscillator to 2-op FM and explicitly rules 4-6-op DX-style FM out of scope\n  \u2014 do not build an operator matrix here.\n- `fmFeedback` \u2014 phase-modulation feedback, cheap and sonically valuable\n- `glide` / portamento time\n- `velToVolume`, `velToFilter` \u2014 velocity mapping (only meaningful once P3a's\n  note cable carries velocity; wire the params now, note in your summary that\n  nothing drives them until P3a)\n\n**Deliberately NOT on this node (justify if you disagree):**\n- Per-oscillator filter (`fmax`/`fmin`/`q`): the plan consolidates all\n  filtering into the separate **Audio Filter** node (\u00a73 Effects). Duplicating\n  a filter inside Oscillator contradicts the consolidation this whole plan is\n  built on. **This is the single most likely place to disagree with a\n  reference implementation that does bundle one \u2014 if you build it, say why.**\n- Per-oscillator amp envelope: same argument, that's the **Envelope**\n  modulator (\u00a73, P3a).\n- Wavetable / drawable waveforms: the plan keeps **Wavetable** a separate node\n  for exactly this reason (different UI, morphing, table previews).\n\n## What to build\n\n### 1. The design document (write this first, before any code)\n\n`docs/plans/audio/audio-node-ui-system.md`. It is the artifact P3a-e sessions\nwill follow, so it must be prescriptive, not exploratory. Cover:\n- The node body **layout grammar**: exact regions in order (title, visualizer,\n  compact param grid, expand affordance, expanded param region, output pin),\n  with concrete pixel sizes chosen against the existing `kPreviewSize` /\n  `kParamWidth` constants so audio nodes sit visually consistent beside\n  visual nodes.\n- The **widget set** and when to use each (compact grid slider, compact\n  dropdown, toggle, the visualizer). Include the rule that every audio param a\n  modulator could drive must still expose a modulator input pin the way\n  `ModSlider` does today \u2014 losing modulation to save space would be a\n  regression, and audio params being modulatable by visual modulators is a\n  core selling point of this app (see `docs/plans/audio/cook-rate-decision.md`).\n- The **visualizer catalogue**: which visualizer each of the plan's 30 node\n  types gets. One line each. This is the table P3 sessions look up.\n- **Right-click menu policy for audio nodes**: which items appear, which are\n  suppressed, and any audio-specific additions.\n- **The cable-type compatibility matrix, as user-facing documentation** \u2014 see\n  the dedicated section below.\n- **Param density policy**: what belongs in the collapsed grid vs. behind\n  expansion, as a rule a future session can apply to a node you never saw.\n- **How density scales down**: a Gain node has one param. State what a\n  one-param audio node looks like under this grammar so it doesn't end up with\n  an absurd amount of chrome around a single slider.\n\n### 1b. Cable compatibility must become visible \u2014 verified real problem\n\nThe user could not work out how to connect Oscillator \u2192 Gain. **The connection\nrule is not broken** \u2014 `IsInputSlotCompatible` (`main.cpp:1623-1628`) correctly\naccepts an `IAudioSource` into any pin whose `AudioInputSlot(slot)` is\nnon-null, and `AUDIOGRAPHTEST` wires that exact chain successfully on every\nrun. The failure is purely that the pin is invisible as an affordance:\n\n- `INode::InputLabel(int)` defaults to `nullptr` (`src/core/INode.h:113`), and\n  **neither `GainNode` nor `AudioOutputNode` overrides it**\n  (`src/nodes/AudioNodes.h`). Their audio input therefore draws as an\n  unlabelled bare dot in the node's top-left corner. Compare `OutputNode`,\n  which labels its pins `\"in\"` / `\"audio\"` (`src/nodes/OutputNode.h`).\n- Link *tinting* by cable type already exists (audio = blue `ImColor(90,150,255)`,\n  note = green `ImColor(90,220,130)`, `main.cpp:13991-13999`) \u2014 but only once a\n  link is already made. Nothing signals compatibility *before* or *during* a\n  drag.\n\nFix as part of the design system, and document the rules:\n\n**The matrix as currently implemented** (`main.cpp:1591-1700`) \u2014 verify this\nstill holds before writing it into the doc, then include it:\n\n| Source | Image pin | Geometry pin | Modulator pin | Audio pin | Note pin |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Image node | yes | no | no | no | no |\n| `IGeometrySource` | no | yes | no | no | no |\n| `IModulator` | no | no | yes | **no** | no |\n| `IAudioSource` | no | no | no | **yes** | no |\n| Note source | no | no | no | no | **yes** |\n\nPlus single-type specialised pins: Camera, Light, Environment (HDRI only),\nPalette (`IPaletteSource`), and the Material/Displacement texture slots.\n\nTwo entries above are deliberate but currently unexplained to the user, and\nthe doc must say so in user-facing language:\n- Audio and Note are **strictly closed** \u2014 no coercion either way.\n- **A visual modulator cannot cable into an audio param.** This is by design\n  (`docs/plans/audio/cook-rate-decision.md`: the intended path is a published\n  atomic read, not a cable) but the mechanism does not exist yet, so the drag\n  silently refuses with no explanation. **Decide and state** whether P2.7\n  should show a \"why\" (a refusal tooltip / status-bar reason) or leave it\n  until the mechanism lands in P3 \u2014 recommendation: show the reason now, since\n  a silent refusal is exactly what cost the user time here.\n\nRequired outcome: every audio and note pin carries a label, and the reason a\nrefused drag was refused is discoverable. Whether that is pin labels alone,\ncompatible-pin highlighting during a drag, a legend, or a tooltip is your\ndesign call \u2014 but a bare unlabelled dot is not acceptable.\n\n### 2. The widget/infrastructure work\n\n- A compact multi-column param grid layout helper, alongside the existing\n  `ModSlider`/`DropdownButton` rather than replacing them (visual nodes keep\n  using the current full-width widgets \u2014 **do not restyle the existing visual\n  node library in this phase**).\n- An inline visualizer widget for audio nodes, and the waveform-trace\n  implementation the Oscillator needs. **RT-safety matters here**: the\n  visualizer must read from the existing `MeterRing` (`src/audio/MeterRing.h`,\n  the audio\u2192main SPSC path) or a main-thread-recomputed preview curve. It\n  must never call into an `AudioNode` from the UI thread, and the audio thread\n  must never touch ImGui. Also honour the plan's \u00a71 drawing rules\n  (`README.md`): decimated rings, ~30 Hz redraw, not per-frame full redraw.\n- A per-node expanded/collapsed flag. `GraphNode` already has `showParams`\n  (`GraphNode.h:36`); add a distinct `showAdvancedParams` rather than\n  overloading it, since \"params visible at all\" and \"showing the full set\" are\n  now two different things. **Persistence caveat, verified:** the patch\n  `flags` line reads exactly three ints via `>>` (`Patch.cpp:296-297`). A\n  fourth int appended is backward-compatible for *reading old patches* (the\n  stream just leaves the 4th variable at its initialized value \u2014 make sure you\n  initialize it), but confirm `ROUNDTRIPTEST`/`PATCHTEST` still pass, and\n  check whether an older build reading a newer patch matters to you.\n\n### 3. The reference node \u2014 the real Oscillator\n\nReplace P2's proof-of-plumbing `OscillatorNode`\n(`src/nodes/AudioNodes.h:20-40`, `src/nodes/AudioNodes.cpp:15-81`) with the\nfull node, built entirely through the new UI system. Keep the existing\ntwo-object structure exactly as it is \u2014 it is correct and RT-safe: the `INode`\nhalf pushes params in `CookIfNeeded`, the `AudioOscillatorNode` half does DSP\nin `ProcessBlock`, communicating only through `ParamMailbox`.\n\nDSP notes:\n- `DspMath::PolyBlepOsc` (`src/audio/DspMath.h`) already provides band-limited\n  `Sine`/`Saw`/`Square`. Pulse-width, triangle, and the noise types are new \u2014\n  implement them there, from primary literature, keeping the existing\n  BLEP-correction approach for anything with a discontinuity.\n- **`ParamMailbox` has a hard limit of `kMaxParams = 64`**\n  (`src/audio/ParamMailbox.h`) and the current node uses index constants\n  defined per-file (`kFreqParam = 0` etc., `AudioNodes.cpp:9-12`). A dense\n  Oscillator will use many more indices. Verify you stay under 64 per node\n  instance, and if the flat-index scheme gets unwieldy, say so rather than\n  quietly exceeding it.\n- Unison means N detuned oscillator instances per voice \u2014 that is a real CPU\n  multiplier. Keep the count fixed-size/preallocated (no allocation in\n  `ProcessBlock`), the same way `VoiceAllocator`\n  (`src/audio/AudioVoice.h`) already sizes its voice vector once at\n  construction.\n\nUpdate `VisitParams` for every new param so save/load round-trips (the\nexisting pattern, `AudioNodes.cpp:71-75`), and update the node's `Help` text\nif the help registry (`main.cpp:5585`) has an entry keyed by type name.\n\n## Clean-room constraint \u2014 unchanged and still binding\n\n**Do not read, open, grep, or reference `/Users/namansoni/BespokeSynth`** or\nany other GPLv3 source, at any point in this phase. Node taxonomy, param\nnames, and general UI layout conventions are not copyrightable and are reused\nfreely across the entire industry \u2014 the researched inventory above is drawn\nfrom public product documentation, deliberately. DSP must be implemented from\nprimary literature (Zavalishin, RBJ cookbook, V\u00e4lim\u00e4ki & Huovilainen for\nPolyBLEP), as every prior phase has done.\n\n## Explicitly out of scope\n\n- Any node other than Oscillator. Gain and Audio Out keep working; migrating\n  them to the new grammar is fine if trivial, but do not start P3's node\n  families.\n- Restyling the existing visual/image/geometry node library.\n- P2.6's audio device settings (`docs/plans/audio/P2.6-audio-settings-prompt.md`)\n  \u2014 separate, independent phase.\n- Export/recording of the live audio graph (planned as P2.7's sibling; the\n  numbering may shift, don't worry about it).\n- 4-6-op FM, wavetables, per-osc filters/envelopes \u2014 see the inventory above.\n\n## Build & verify\n\n```bash\ncmake --build build -j\"$(sysctl -n hw.ncpu)\"\n```\n\n```bash\n.claude/skills/run-infinite-hygiene/driver.sh\n```\n\nBaseline is **39/40 passing**. The only expected failure is `PHASEATEST`\n(a pre-existing, unrelated `\"Smooth\"` node-name collision the user has\nalready fixed elsewhere \u2014 **do not attempt to fix it, and do not report it as\na regression**). Pay particular attention to `ROUNDTRIPTEST` and `PATCHTEST`\nif you add the fourth `flags` int, and to `AUDIOGRAPHTEST` (audio\ndelete-crash) since you are changing an audio node's lifetime surface.\n\n```bash\nINFINITE_DSPTEST=1 ./build/Infinite.app/Contents/MacOS/Infinite\n```\nMust still end `DSPTEST OK` (7 checks). If you extend `PolyBlepOsc`, add\ncoverage there for the new waveforms \u2014 a zero-crossing/frequency check and a\npeak-amplitude check, matching the existing fixture's style.\n\nFinally, launch the app and confirm by eye: spawn an Oscillator, check the\ncollapsed grid reads clearly, the visualizer animates, expansion reveals the\nfull set, and **verify the right-click menu offers no viewport/new-window\nitems**. Wire Oscillator \u2192 Gain \u2192 Audio Out and confirm it still makes sound.\n\n## Sources for the param research\n\n- [Bitwig Polymer](https://www.bitwig.com/polymer/) and [Bitwig user guide \u2014 Synth](https://www.bitwig.com/userguide/latest/synth/)\n- [Kilohearts Phase Plant docs](https://kilohearts.com/docs/phase_plant)\n- [Omnisphere \u2014 Oscillator Unison](https://support.spectrasonics.net/manual/Omnisphere/edit_page/oscillator/page22.html)\n- [Steinberg HALion \u2014 FM synthesis](https://www.steinberg.help/r/halion/7.1/en/halion/topics/editing_zones/fm_synthesis_c.html)\n- [SynthEdit HD Oscillator](https://synthedit-help.co.uk/hd-oscillator/oscillators/)\n- [Ableton Live instrument reference](https://www.ableton.com/en/manual/live-instrument-reference/)"
